        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260509-hantavirus-hit-cruise-ship-heads-for-canary-islands-to-evacuate-passengers",
        "orario": "10:39",
        "timestamp": 1778315994,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Hantavirus-hit cruise ship heads for Canary Islands to evacuate passengers Europe Issued on: 09/05/2026 - 10:39 Spanish authorities on Friday were preparing to receive more than 140 passengers and crew members on board a hantavirus-stricken cruise ship headed for the Canary Islands, where health officials have said they will perform careful evacuations. The vessel is expected to arrive Sunday at the Spanish island of Tenerife, the passengers will then be transported to the airport and flown back to their respective countries. Russia marks Victory Day with scaled-back parade 09/05/2026 Europe UK: The end of the traditional two-party system? Starmer faces crushing defeat in local polls 08/05/2026 Europe Substantial win for Nigel Farage's Reform UK in local elections 08/05/2026 Europe Energy security vs climate crisis: Norway reopens three old gas fields 08/05/2026 Europe Keir Starmer's Labour braces for heavy losses in UK local elections 08/05/2026 Europe Russia and Ukraine trade major attacks despite Victory Day ceasefire 08/05/2026 Europe 'Ici c'est Paris': Defending champions PSG 'on the verge of making history' 07/05/2026 Sport 3 patients are being evacuated to Europe from ship with hantavirus outbreak 06/05/2026 Europe War in Ukraine: Russia attacks east and south Ukraine with over 100 drones 06/05/2026 Europe"
